{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:100821",
  "title": "Critical: php8.4 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-23 12:06:29"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-24 06:08:14"
  },
  "severity": "Critical",
  "description": "PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* php: PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during PATH_INFO correction (CVE-2026-129538)\n\n* php: Timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote  code execution (CVE-2026-129496)\n\n* php: Double free during DOM XML serialization) (CVE-2026-129501)\n\n* php: PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local  privilege escalation (CVE-2026-129291)\n\n* php: PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP request body) (CVE-2026-129289)\n\n* php: PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user and script fields) (CVE-2026-129292)\n\n* php: PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm downgrade (CVE-2026-128090)\n\n* php: SOAP information disclosure through malformed array dimensions) (CVE-2026-15353)\n\n* php: SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity references (CVE-2026-129506)\n\n* php: Partially overwritten session files can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-126714)\n\n* php: Session serializer mismatch can lead to remote code execution (CVE-2026-115560)\n\n* php: Use-after-free after interrupted session shutdown (CVE-2026-129481)\n\n* php: Mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data in plaintext (CVE-2026-128064)\n\n* php: Denial of service through folded HTTP response headers (CVE-2026-127960)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* php8.4: Rebase PHP to 8.4.28 in 10.3.z (JIRA:Rocky Linux-310446)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
